course: dictionary
lesson: 6863
title: Overcome: beat it or be beaten
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overcome has more than one meaning, so the words around it give you the clue. To overcome a problem or a fear is to deal with it and beat it. In «nothing could overcome his stage-fright», the clue is stage-fright, a fear, so overcome means something strong enough to beat it.
explain: Overcome can also mean to defeat an enemy. When a hero overcomes a villain, the villain loses. The past tense is overcame, as in «she overcame her fear of water», which tells you the fear was beaten in the past.
explain: Be careful with «be overcome». To be overcome by a strong feeling, smoke or heat is to be made weak or helpless by it. «He was overcome with emotion» does not mean he won a fight. It means the feeling was too strong for him. Always ask: did someone win, or were they made helpless?
fact: Overcome is a verb, and it can also be an adjective: «The smoke made her overcome» is not correct, but «she was overcome by smoke» is.
fact: «Overcome» means to beat a problem, a fear or an enemy.
fact: «Overcame» is the past tense of overcome: «she overcame her fear of water».
fact: To be overcome means to be made weak or helpless by a strong feeling, smoke or heat.
fact: Safety rule: smoke can overcome people, so get low, keep your head down and get out.
exercise: «She overcame her fear of water.» What does overcame mean here? | Ran away from the water | *Beat her fear | Was frightened by a bird | Went swimming in the sea
exercise: In a fire, people can be overcome by smoke. What does this mean? | Lit up by the smoke | *Made weak and helpless by the smoke | Chased out of the room by smoke | Painted grey, like the smoke
exercise: «Nothing could overcome his stage-fright.» Which word is the clue that overcome means beat? | His | Could | *Stage-fright | Nothing
test: «The knight overcame the dragon at last.» What does overcame mean here? | Fed | *Defeated | Followed | Woke
test: «Mia was overcome with joy when she won.» What does overcome with joy mean? | *Made helpless by a strong feeling | Tired from running | Angry with her team | Bored of the game
exam: Which sentence means someone beat their fear? | *Anna overcame her fear of heights. | Anna overheard the fear. | Anna overflowed with fear. | Anna overslept after the fear.
